1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,033
The consequences came in the form of a school report.

2
00:00:03,033 --> 00:00:13,100
A kindergarten headmaster, a therapist, and a poet were listed as beneficiaries of the study, and not one of them had ever been asked.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:18,154
“Admittedly, that is a fault of ours,” Maya said.

4
00:00:18,154 --> 00:00:24,922
“We cater to the people who read reports, not to the people inside them.”

5
00:00:24,922 --> 00:00:30,341
The first acknowledgement arrived with a loaf of bread and a jar of jam.

6
00:00:30,341 --> 00:00:41,778
A silvery morning, a rainbow over the sports hall, and the smell of a loaf cooling on a windowsill made the whole argument feel splendid and slightly unreal.

7
00:00:41,778 --> 00:00:47,806
“Sugar, honey, candy, biscuits,” Lin wrote.

8
00:00:47,806 --> 00:00:54,240
“The vocabulary of comfort is doing the work of the vocabulary of proof.”

9
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:57,779
He was frustrated by the tiny scope.

10
00:00:57,779 --> 00:01:05,242
Young volunteers wanted a glorious result, and the darkness of the numbers was itself the answer.

11
00:01:05,242 --> 00:01:21,567
“A peach and an orange are not the same fruit,” Maya said, “even when both are sweet.” Furniture was moved to make room for a new shelf, and the glow of the reading lamp became the room's only decoration.

12
00:01:21,567 --> 00:01:28,920
The children taught themselves faster than the adults did; the method itself was not the problem.

13
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:36,073
A bushy hedge, a tomato plant, and a rose in a wine bottle stood on the windowsill.

14
00:01:36,073 --> 00:01:41,557
“A teen can tell when a greeting is automatic,” the therapist said.

15
00:01:41,557 --> 00:01:49,175
“That is the awful part.” A dark joke about the yellow folder did not help.

16
00:01:49,175 --> 00:01:58,342
A scholastic prize, a sandwich, and a shine of sweat on the window told him nothing about what the children had actually learned.

17
00:01:58,342 --> 00:02:05,370
They wrote a philosophical page about measurement and a sleepy one about the six forms of feedback.

18
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:12,218
Then they stopped, because the poetry of the thing was becoming a substitute for the thing.

19
00:02:12,218 --> 00:02:26,149
“From here on,” Lin said, “we lead with what we do not know.” All of it was given to the school without conditions; however, there was a lot they could not hear from the corridor.

20
00:02:26,149 --> 00:02:35,287
So this was the other side of the yellow folder: a fortunate habit of writing things up, and nobody up there to read them.

21
00:02:35,287 --> 00:02:41,322
A movie would have ended here; a project does not.
